Z||000075||SLAMMED87GT||12-17-2001||12:48 PM||||Well- I am using thr bra on my '87 GT to cover up some chips, but quite honestly, I don't think it looks that bad. Heck, didn't seem to matter at the shows either, I still ended up placing!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>If you are going to have a bra on you car you need to spray it with vinyl protectant. It looks so much better this way and also protects it as well. Here is a pic of mine.<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fiero10-01,3.jpg"> <P>I do plan on taking it off after I get my front spoiler and have it painted.<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Pfierosig2_1.jpg"> <P><P>------------------<BR>3" Drop, 17" Primax 618s/Nitto450 205/40, 4" Monza exhaust, Mudstain decklid scoop, 7" wing stands, Clear front and rear lights, custom interior, all options...that's all hehe.||||reg||6
Z||000076||rogergarrison||12-17-2001||01:28 PM||||Most of the girls I date are too small chested to need a bra, Im just not that attracted by them, Im a leg & face guy. Oh, and I agree to not wanting them on a car either.||||reg||1
Z||000077||MinnGreenGT||12-17-2001||02:17 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by SLAMMED87GT:<BR><B>If you are going to have a bra on you car you need to spray it with vinyl protectant. It looks so much better this way and also protects it as well...</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>The Saddleman Corp/LeBra states specifically in the instructions that you DO NOT put "vinyl protectant" on the cover- and that if you do it voids the warranty.  It will look nice, but it seals the vinyl from any airflow and hinders it's ability to dry after rain/washing. Eventually it will get a buildup of moisture and cause mold/mildew and begin to stink and cause a deterioration of the fabric itself.  The instructions stated specifically to only clean them with soapy water and to rinse thoroughly.||||reg||1
Z||000078||SLAMMED87GT||12-17-2001||02:26 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by MinnGreenGT:<BR><B> The Saddleman Corp/LeBra states specifically in the instructions that you DO NOT put "vinyl protectant" on the cover- and that if you do it voids the warranty.  It will look nice, but it seals the vinyl from any airflow and hinders it's ability to dry after rain/washing. Eventually it will get a buildup of moisture and cause mold/mildew and begin to stink and cause a deterioration of the fabric itself.  The instructions stated specifically to only clean them with soapy water and to rinse thoroughly.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I have been using a protector on my bra ever since I started wearing one and never had any problem?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>But I also wash my Fiero at least once a week, usually twice a week and new protectant is put on. I also have a Wolf bra, but being it's probably made out of the same components.<P>BTW-Are going to the X-mas party? I will be there! See Ya later.<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Pfierosig2_1.jpg"> <P><P>------------------<BR>3" Drop, 17" Primax 618s/Nitto450 205/40, 4" Monza exhaust, Mudstain decklid scoop, 7" wing stands, Clear front and rear lights, custom interior, all options...that's all hehe.||||reg||1
